DESCRIPTION:(1353) Maartje hides a magnitude 12.8 star\, seen from Nalgonda
 .\nThe predicted edge passes 17 km to the NNW\, so a miss is likely — bu
 t a chord from near the edge is the most valuable observation of all.\nClo
 sest approach 01:53:26 IST\, give or take 1 s. The star is 17° up in the 
 ENE · dark sky.\nIt fades 3.2 magnitudes for up to 1.7 s on the centre li
 ne\, and the path is 39 km wide\, give or take 23 km.\nThe map\, the finde
 r chart and the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroid?e=2027-08-3
 0-1353-maartje-857280
